  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Cambodia Malaria Elimination Project 2 (CMEP 2)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Cambodia):  The Cambodia Malaria Elimination Project 2 (CMEP2) is a new activity that continues the work of  CMEP1&apos;s objectives to implement malaria elimination interventions and prevention of reintroduction of malaria in the six target provinces. The activity is aligned with the Cambodia National Malaria Control Program&apos;s revised Malaria Elimination Action Framework phase two (MEAF II from 2021-2025). ..USAID and the U.S. President&apos;s Malaria Initiative (PMI) provided decisive support to malaria elimination through past activities such as CMEP1. USAID designed CMEP2 to leverage CMEP1&apos;s successes. USAID  awarded this contract through a competitive process in which the offeror with the best value to the U.S. government was selected..The activity falls under the administration&apos;s priority of &quot;advancing global health security as well as detecting, preventing, controlling, and treating disease and pandemics.&quot; In addition, this activity supports the ICS Mission Objective 2.3, Sub-objective 2.3.1, &quot;By 2024, quality of and access to priority health services improved.&quot; It also supports the Indo-Pacific Strategy Goal 2: &quot;Build connections within and beyond the region.&quot; The activity supports the FY 2022 - 2026 State-USAID Joint Strategy Plan Strategic Objective 1.1, &quot;Leadership in strengthening global health security&quot; and aligns with the East Asia Joint Regional Strategy&apos;s Objective 2.1, &quot;Build sustainable and resilient health systems to detect and respond to emerging challenges, including current and future pandemics&quot;. This activity is included in the FY 2022 Malaria Operational Plan and is fully aligned with the PMI goals... ...</narrative>
  </description>
